*.pyc
!report/figures/*.png
fisher_analysis/
.venv/
__pycache__/

# Local research archive. The complete exploration tree, including historical
# results, remains on disk but is intentionally excluded from the university
# repository. Canonical university code must live outside this directory.
/exploration/

# Local rendering and scratch artifacts.
/tmp/

# Per-task shards of the parallel sampled factorial: intermediate files that the
# combined CSVs already contain, and re-derivable by rerunning the driver.
exploration/results/**/shards/

# Per-update traces of the sampled factorial. These are the bulk of a run (320 MB
# of checkpoints at 2000 updates, past GitHub's 100 MB per-file limit) and are not
# needed to reproduce any reported number: sampled_endpoints.csv regenerates
# sampled_method_summaries.csv and sampled_paired_differences.csv byte-identically.
# Rerun run_sampled_damped.py to recover the traces when a diagnostic needs them.
exploration/results/**/sampled_checkpoints.csv
exploration/results/**/sampled_missing_state_audit.csv

# The budget sweep's trace, excluded for the same reason under a different name:
# 26 MB of per-run rows, of which only the handoff checkpoint is ever read.
# budget_endpoints.csv alone regenerates budget_contrasts.csv and every column of
# budget_summaries.csv except pi1_good_at_handoff, which needs the trace; both
# committed CSVs already hold the derived values. Rerun budget_sweep.py to
# recover it.
exploration/results/**/budget_checkpoints.csv

# Per-run .npz archive dumps of the tabular_mdp trap experiments: 1.23 GB across
# five archives/ directories, and the largest single item in the tree by an order
# of magnitude. These are intermediate per-seed dumps, not reported quantities --
# the endpoint and summary CSVs alongside them already hold every value the
# reports cite. Rerun the corresponding driver to regenerate an archive when a
# diagnostic needs the raw arrays. The result arrays that ARE cited
# (categorical_bandit paper/eta, acrobot fisher_spectra) stay committed.
exploration/results/**/archives/

# Prose and typeset output. The experiments' numbers live in the committed CSV
# and JSON; the writing that interprets them is drafted outside this repo, so
# only data is versioned here. Files already tracked before this rule (the
# per-package README.md, sampled_two_state.tex, two_state_geometry.tex) are
# unaffected -- .gitignore does not untrack, and they stay under version control.
*.tex
*.md
!REPOSITORY_INVENTORY.md
*.pdf

# LaTeX build byproducts, orphaned by the rule above: these are regenerated from
# the .tex sources on every compile and are meaningless without them.
*.aux
*.toc
*.out
*.fls
*.fdb_latexmk
*.synctex.gz
*.bbl
*.blg
*.lof
*.lot
